{"id": "valpaca0019", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "All right, so the first thing you want to do is get a whole pig. It' s really important that it's not just any old pig, but one that's been raised specifically for roasting. You can find these at your local butcher or farm supply store. Once you have your pig, you'll need some equipment to get it ready for roasting. First up, you'll need a spit, which is basically a long metal rod that goes through the center of the pig. This will help keep the pig steady while it roast s. You'll also need a rot isserie motor, which is what makes the sp it turn slowly over the heat source. If you don't have access to a rotisserie motor, don't worry, there are other ways to achieve this effect using different types of equipment. Next, you'll need a heat source. You can use a grill, smoker, or even an oven if you prefer. Just make sure whatever you're using can handle high temperatures and direct contact with meat. Now let's talk about preparation. Start by truss ing the pig, which means tying its legs together and securing the skin to the body with string or twine. This helps maintain shape during cooking. Then season the pig thoroughly with salt, pepper, and any other spices", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
