{"id": "valpaca0067", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 15, "onset_chunk": 14, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Sure, I can give you a recipe for Tunisian Ka mounia. It's a traditional dish from the region of Keb il in Tunisia, and it' s made with lamb or goat meat that's slow-co oked with spices and served with bread. Here's what you'll need: one pound of lamb shoulder cut into small pieces, two onions finely chopped, three garlic clo ves minced, one cup of tomato pure e, half a cup of water, two tea spo ons of olive oil, a quarter teaspoon of saffron threads so aked in warm water, one teaspoon of ground cumin, one tea spoon of ground coriander, one teaspo on of paprika, salt to taste, fresh mint leaves for garnish, and some toasted pine nuts for serving. First, heat the olive oil in a large pot over medium heat. Add the onions and cook until they are soft and golden brown, about five minutes. Then add the garlic and cook for another minute.N ext, add the lamb pieces, stir well to coat them with the oil, and cook until they are browned on all sides, which should take about ten minutes. Once the lamb is browned, add the tomato pure e, cumin, coriander, pa prika, salt, and soaked saff", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
