{"id": "valpaca0167", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, I think it' s a very interesting question to ask whether or not we have a moral obligation. I think if you look at history, the people who had the greatest impact on humanity were always the ones who looked out for something bigger than themselves, who took risks and made sacrifices for the good of all of us. And that's really what makes progress possible. So I think we should absolutely continue to explore space. But in order to do that, we need to make sure that we're doing everything we can to solve the problems here on Earth. We need to make sure that we're investing in things like renewable energy and sustainable agriculture so that we can create a future where everyone has access to clean water and food.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 35, "carrier_ended": null}
